WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.030
Thank you very much, Shirley.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.850
This is a very proud
and a very happy moment.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.245
And the winner is Linda Hunt.

00:00:10.245 --> 00:00:13.710
[APPLAUSE]

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.340
This is extraordinary.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:47.600
There was an Indonesian phrase
in the film, which translates

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.340
into English as,
"water from the moon"

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.730
and it means that
which is unattainable,

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:03.370
the impossible, that which
one can never have or know.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.890
Making The Year of
Living Dangerously for me

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.700
was "water from the moon."

00:01:12.165 --> 00:01:14.145
Thank you.

00:01:14.145 --> 00:01:17.115
[APPLAUSE]

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:27.980
And the winner is Marlee Matlin.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.452
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.210
I am --

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.250
I just want to thank
a lot of people.

00:02:08.637 --> 00:02:10.970
To tell you the truth, I
didn't prepare for this speech.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:16.660
But I definitely want to thank
the Academy and its members.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:24.030
And I want to thank my mother
and father, Eric, Marc, Gloria,

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.070
Zachary, and Liz.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.250
They're here tonight with me.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.750
And I just want to
thank all of you.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.766
I love you.

00:02:34.766 --> 00:02:38.077
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:44.044
Ladies and gentlemen,
Christopher Reeve.

00:02:44.044 --> 00:02:47.488
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:48.964 --> 00:02:49.948
Thank you.

00:02:55.852 --> 00:02:57.328
Thank you very much.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.692
Thank you.

00:03:05.692 --> 00:03:07.168
Thank you very much.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.810
What you probably
don't know is that I

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:23.390
left New York last
September, and I just

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:26.048
arrived here this morning.

00:03:26.048 --> 00:03:29.380
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.712
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:40.152
And I'm glad I did
because I wouldn't

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.110
have missed this kind of
welcome for the world.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:42.680
Thank you.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:55.635
When I was a kid, my friends
and I went to the movies just

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:56.135
for fun.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:05.050
But then we saw Kubrick's,
Dr. Strangelove.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:10.470
It started us thinking about the
madness of nuclear destruction.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.450
Stanley Kramer's,
The Defiant Ones

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:16.170
taught us about race relations.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.029
And we began to
realize that films

00:04:18.029 --> 00:04:21.560
could deal with social issues.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.340
Now when you look at
films like Platoon,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:32.470
and Philadelphia, Lorenzo's Oil,
you realize the power of film

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.230
to present painful but
important issues to the public.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:44.250
So here are just a
few more of the motion

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:50.720
pictures that have courageously
put social issues ahead

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.800
of box office success.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:05:00.100
They've enlightened us,
they've challenged us,

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.920
and they've given us the
opportunity to learn.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.670
Hollywood needs to do more.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.245
Let's continue to take risks.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.720
Let's tackle the
issues in many ways.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.130
In many ways our film
community can do it better

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.920
than anyone else.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:28.390
There is no challenge,
artistic or otherwise,

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.478
that we can't meet.

00:05:30.478 --> 00:05:32.973
Thank you.

00:05:32.973 --> 00:05:36.466
[APPLAUSE]

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:48.061
Ladies and gentlemen, here are
Seth Rogen and Michael J. Fox.

00:05:48.061 --> 00:05:51.540
[JAZZY MUSIC]

00:05:58.995 --> 00:06:02.474
[APPLAUSE]

00:06:08.885 --> 00:06:10.510
I'm going to pretend
half that applause

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:15.510
is for me even though I
know deep down it is not.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:16.880
Some of it was for you.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.930
You think like, 30%
of it was for me?

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.030
Some of it was for you.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.800
Great.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.770
Either way I'm at the
Oscars with Michael J. Fox,

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:27.795
a DeLorean, while
wearing future shoes.

00:06:31.912 --> 00:06:33.870
All I have to do is sing
"The Schuyler Sisters"

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.578
song from Hamilton in
front of the world,

00:06:35.578 --> 00:06:37.680
and I will have completed
my entire bucket list.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.320
(SINGING) Look
around, look around

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:48.120
at how lucky we are
to be alive right now!

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:48.900
Angelica!

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.810
Eliza!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:56.580
And Peggy!

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.838
Look around, look around --

00:06:58.838 --> 00:07:00.130
OK we can't do the whole thing.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:00.630
OK, fine.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.588
I don't want to be in
the room when it happens.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:03.430
OK.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.382
Let's keep going.

00:07:04.382 --> 00:07:06.340
We're here to present
the award for Achievement

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.552
in Film Editing.

00:07:07.552 --> 00:07:09.760
Since we're talking about
influences and influencers,

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.273
I want to mention how much
we all owe to editors.

00:07:12.273 --> 00:07:13.690
There isn't a
nominee here tonight

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.840
that doesn't depend on editors
to show off their best work.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:20.602
Here are the nominees for
Achievement in Film Editing.

00:07:20.602 --> 00:07:23.899
[APPLAUSE]

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.130
Short films allow for new
voices to be seen and heard

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.900
without the constraints
of budget or permission.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.810
I've seen these films
and they are beautiful.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:43.610
And if you haven't
seen it, come see it.

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.780
[APPLAUSE]

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:48.460
Here are the nominees for
Best Live Action Short Film.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:53.640
The Oscar goes to

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.500
The Neighbors' Window.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.500
[APPLAUSE]

